    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear tactical mandate: exploit favorable matchups against vulnerable pitching. Our primary anchors are **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) and **Trea Turner** (79.40), who draw the most favorable situational conditions of the day. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from a massive 19% boost due to the matchup against Dobnak, bolstered by a +14% platoon edge and favorable wind conditions that push him to the top of our daily hierarchy. Similarly, **Trea Turner** is locked in to exploit the favorable 5.23 xERA of Bieber; with his elite sprint speed serving as our primary vehicle for points in the scarce SB category, he is a locked-in must-start. **Kyle Schwarber** also benefits from the same Bieber matchup, maintaining a strong 78.21 rating by securing the leadoff spot and maximizing the offensive upside of the favorable pitching environment.\n\nWhile our top-tier plays are secure, we are closely monitoring the lineup statuses of **Junior Caminero** (60.46) and **Yordan Alvarez** (65.05). Both are assumed to be in the two/three-hole slots, and their elite xwOBA metrics make them essential cornerstones of the lineup despite the lack of official confirmation. Conversely, we have opted to bench **Josh Smith** (32.43). Despite his versatility, he failed to cross our 40.0 efficiency threshold; the combination of a tough matchup against Luzardo\u2019s 3.20 xERA and a poor batting order position relegated him to the bench. We remain cautious with **Dillon Dingler** (40.50), whose score remains near our minimum floor due to a disadvantageous dynamic platoon against Webb; he stays in the lineup strictly to preserve our game caps, but he is the first candidate for mid-game substitution should we need a defensive or pinch-hitting upgrade.",
